{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791828639,"nonce":"09TMuLsuAUoV/RklGGb2rwy2ADk=","title":"Support declarative repeated items in Command","message":"Command.render indexes authored Component.children, and CommandGroup.items only examines its direct authored children. An HXX \u003cfor\u003e creates ashui.ui.For (a Div), so \u003ccommand-list\u003e\u003ccommand-group\u003e\u003cfor {tool in tools}\u003e\u003ccommand-item .../\u003e\u003c/for\u003e\u003c/command-group\u003e\u003c/command-list\u003e is not indexed. Search, the group's visibility, and keyboard selection consequently miss its items.\n\nChimpMonk's editor/ui/CommandCenter.hx currently passes concrete CommandItem arrays into CommandGroup/CommandList and keeps each row in HXX. This exception prevents using ordinary declarative repetition for a shared tool catalog.\n\nIndex repeated items after their children mount, update the index as the list changes, and preserve active selection when possible. Verify search, empty/group visibility, keyboard selection and owner disposal for static and signal-driven HXX \u003cfor\u003e children.","files":null}]}